  "answer_text": "You can download the latest version of Python from the **official Python website**:\n\n\ud83d\udd17 **https://www.python.org/downloads/**\n\nThe latest version is **Python 3.14.5**, and Python source code and installers are available for download for all versions on the official site.\n\nPython 3.14.5 was released on **May 10, 2026**.\n\nHere are some highlights about what's available:\n\n- **Windows:** The installer for Windows is being replaced by a new install manager, which can be installed from the Windows Store or from its download page.\n- **macOS & Linux:** Installers and source code are available directly from the downloads page.\n- **Source Code:** For most Unix systems, you must download and compile the source code. The same source code archive can also be used to build the Windows and Mac versions, and is the starting point for ports to all other platforms.\n\nSome notable features in the Python 3.14 series include:\n- Free-threaded Python is officially supported, and template string literals (t-strings) for custom string processing using the familiar syntax of f-strings have been added.\n- A new module `compression.zstd` providing support for the Zstandard compression algorithm.\n\nSimply head to **https://www.python.org/downloads/**, and the site will automatically suggest the best installer for your operating system!",
